🐛 Bug

After training an simple model successfully using libtorch C++ and saved as a .pt file.   Loading the model and trying to test the model with an input tensor gave me c10 error.
To Reproduce
Steps to reproduce the behavior:

Used torch::save() to save a trained model
Used OpenCV 4.0.1 to load an image, resize it, convert it to tensor using torch::from_blob
Create my model object ConvNet model(image.channels(), image.rows, image.cols); then using torch::load(model, save_model.pt) to load the saved model. Loading model and tensor on either gpu or cpu is fine, but when forward the tensor, it gave me error during the first convolution in my model's forward process.

** I found out the problem happened after calling the first convolution process in my model's forward process.  Wondering could it be due to the difference between tensor's dimension? I didn't expend another dimension during training process, but according to what i see here seems like we will expend another dimension, then feed in to the model.
**Update: I used a docker container which includes both built from source libtorch and opencv, which doesn't gave me the error in Windows.  Also, how come the built from source libtorch in ubuntu gave me detailed error information than in Windows.  Did I accidentally built libtorch as debug?
How I prepare input data for training:
